Solve algebraically:
\[
{ }_{n} C_{2}=3 n+4
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{array}{rl}
\frac{n!}{(n-2)!2!} & =3 n+4 \\
\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)!}{\frac{(n-2)!}{n(n-1)}} & =2!(3 n+4) \\
n^{2}-n & =6 n+8 \\
n^{2}-7 n-8 & =0 \\
(n-8)(n+1) & =0 \\
n=8 & n=-1
\end{array}
\]
